# Jarvis-like AI Voice Assistant — Implementation Plan

## Problem & Goal

The Speak-Sync app has a full AI Voice pipeline (STT → NLU → TTS) and a beautiful Gemini-style voice overlay, but **the AI currently does nothing actionable**. The Gateway's [converse()](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/flutter/speak_sync_app/lib/core/services/voice_service.dart#197-244) is a placeholder that echoes transcripts, and the AI Brain's NLU detects intents but never executes them. 

**Goal:** Turn the AI into a Jarvis-like assistant that actually **controls the app via voice** — creating tasks, logging habits, scheduling events, changing profile, generating reports, etc. — in a natural, conversational style with low friction.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **This is a large, multi-service change** spanning AI Brain Service (Python), Gateway Service (Node.js), and Flutter app. The plan is designed as **Phase 2 first** (backend action engine) so we can verify intent→action mapping works before touching the frontend.

> [!WARNING] 
> **LLM Dependency:** The action execution depends on the NLU service correctly parsing intents. The quality of intent detection relies on the Llama-3.3-70b model via OpenRouter. Error handling and fallback paths are included in the design.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Flutter App                                              │
│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐           │
│  │ GeminiVoiceOverlay                         │           │
│  │  Record → VoiceService.converse()          │           │
│  │  ← Action result + AI spoken response      │           │
│  └──────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘           │
└─────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┘
                      │ POST /api/gateway/ai/converse
                      ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Gateway Service (Node.js)                                │
│  ai.service.ts → converse()                               │
│    1. Forward audio to AI Brain /conversation/voice       │
│    2. Receive intent + entities + action_result            │
│    3. If action needed → call Scheduler/Lifestyle APIs     │
│    4. Return response + action_result to Flutter           │
└──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘
                   │
         ┌─────────┼──────────┐
         ▼         ▼          ▼
┌────────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌──────────┐
│ AI Brain   │ │Scheduler│ │Lifestyle │
│ (Python)   │ │(Node.js)│ │(Python)  │
│ STT→NLU→  │ │Tasks    │ │Habits    │
│ Action→TTS │ │Events   │ │Food/Water│
│            │ │Categor. │ │Exercise  │
└────────────┘ └────────┘ │Sleep/etc.│
                           └──────────┘
```

---

## Proposed Changes

### AI Brain Service — Action Execution Engine

This is the core new component. After NLU detects an intent, the action executor decides what API action to take and formats the parameters.

#### [NEW] [action_executor_service.py](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/services/action_executor_service.py)

New service that maps detected intents to structured action payloads:

- **Input:** NLU result ([intent](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/api/routes/chat.py#309-335), `domain`, [entities](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/api/routes/chat.py#89-128), [confidence](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/services/voice_service.py#218-248))
- **Output:** Action descriptor with [service](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/main.py#201-224), `method`, `endpoint`, `payload`, `confirmation_text`
- Implements the **"Missing Data" Strategy** — fills in smart defaults (today's date, neutral mood, etc.) when user doesn't provide everything, instead of asking interrogative follow-ups
- Maps every app intent to its backend API call:

| Intent | Service | API Call | Example |
|--------|---------|----------|---------|
| `create_task` | Scheduler | `POST /api/tasks` | "Add buy groceries to my tasks" |
| `update_task` | Scheduler | `PUT /api/tasks/:id` | "Mark my workout task as done" |
| `delete_task` | Scheduler | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | "Delete the meeting task" |
| `query_schedule` | Scheduler | `GET /api/tasks` | "What are my tasks for today?" |
| `create_event` | Scheduler | `POST /api/events` | "Schedule a meeting tomorrow at 3pm" |
| `log_exercise` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/exercise` | "I just finished a 30 min run" |
| `log_food` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/food` | "I had rice and dal for lunch" |
| `log_water` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/water` | "Just drank a glass of water" |
| `log_sleep` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/sleep` | "I slept at 11pm, woke up at 7am" |
| `log_expense` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/finance` | "Spent 500 on groceries" |
| `track_habit` | Lifestyle | `POST /api/habits/:id/log` | "I meditated for 20 minutes" |
| `greeting` | None | N/A | "Hey!" → AI greets back |

---

#### [MODIFY] [nlu_service.py](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/services/nlu_service.py)

- **Expand `INTENT_CATEGORIES`** to include: `create_event`, `update_event`, `delete_event`, `query_habits`, `log_food`, `log_study`, `update_profile`, `get_report`
- **Improve system prompt** for better conversational tone matching the user's examples (no interrogation, infer missing data, conversational follow-ups)
- **Add context enrichment** — pass current time, time of day (for greeting style), first-time flag

---

#### [MODIFY] [conversation_service.py](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/services/conversation_service.py)

- **Add action execution step** after NLU, before TTS:
  ```
  STT → NLU → ACTION_EXECUTOR → GENERATE_RESPONSE (with action result) → TTS
  ```
- **Add first-time greeting logic**: Track `is_first_interaction` per user in session, deliver onboarding greeting on first click
- **Add multi-turn context**: When action executor needs more info (e.g., which task to delete when user has many), store pending_action in session and ask a soft follow-up
- **Include `action_result`** in the response payload so Gateway/Flutter can show action confirmations

---

### Gateway Service — Proper Conversation Routing

#### [MODIFY] [ai.service.ts](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/gateway-service/src/services/ai.service.ts)

- **Replace placeholder [converse()](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/flutter/speak_sync_app/lib/core/services/voice_service.dart#197-244)** with proper call to AI Brain's `/api/ai/conversation/voice` endpoint
- **Add action routing**: When AI Brain returns an action payload, execute it against the appropriate backend service (Scheduler or Lifestyle) using existing service clients
- **Return structured result** to Flutter including: `transcript`, `response_text`, `audio_base64`, `action_result` (what was created/updated/deleted)

#### [MODIFY] [ai.routes.ts](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/gateway-service/src/routes/ai.routes.ts)

- **Update `/converse` endpoint** to pass `user_id` from JWT token to AI Brain service
- **Add `action_result`** to the response body

